standardised conditions. Examples include curry
powder and thyme. On the other hand unprocessed
spices are not necessarily produced under standardised
conditions. These types of spices are more commonly
used in African cultural food preparation. For example
in Nigeria, “yaji” (Suya spice) is an unprocessed spice
that is traditionally used to prepare a meat delicacy
called suya by the hausa ethnic group (Okonkwo,
1987). Another example is the pepper soup spice
which is used to prepare pepper soup; a delicacy
usually taken among the southern ethnic group of the
country especially the Yorubas.

